      <div type="clause" n="47">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 47</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="47" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="80" ed="#liebermann"/>XLIII. Gif mon men eage ofáslea, geselle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_47.lnote.oe.3"/> him mon LX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_47.lnote.oe.4"/> scill'<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_47.lnote.oe.5"/> ⁊ VI<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_47.lnote.oe.6"/> scill' ⁊ VI<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_47.lnote.oe.7"/> pæningas ⁊ ðriddan dǽl pæninges<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_47.lnote.oe.8"/> to bote.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="47" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="80" ed="#liebermann"/>XLIII. Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_47.lnote.oe.4-2"/> men his eage ofaslea, gesylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_47.lnote.oe.1"/> him mon LX scll' ⁊ VI scll' ⁊ VI peningas ⁊ ðriddan dæl peniges<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_47.lnote.oe.5-2"/> to bote.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="47" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="80" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf mon men eage ofaslea, gesylle him mon syxti scill' ⁊ syx scill' ⁊ six penegas ⁊ ðriddan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_47.lnote.oe.1-2"/> dæl peniges to bote.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="47" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="81" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_47.lnote.oe.3-2"/> alii ofaslea<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_47.lnote.oe.4-3"/> (crepet) oculum, soluat ei LXVI sol. et VI d. et terciam partem unius denarii (que<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_47.lnote.oe.5-3"/> est triens).</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="86" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif mon men eage<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#Af_47.attnote.fn.6"/> ofáslea, geselle him mon LX scill' ⁊ VI scill' ⁊ VI pæningas<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#Af_47.attnote.fn.7"/> ⁊ ðriddan dǽl pæninges to bote.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="50" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="350" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XLIII} Gif mon men eage ofáslea, geselle him mon LX scill' ⁊ VI scill' ⁊ VI pæningas, ⁊ ðriddan dæl pæninges to bote.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="81" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_47.lnote.de.1"/> man jemandem ein Auge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_47.lnote.de.2"/> ausschlägt, gebe man ihm 60 Schill. und 6 Schill. und 6<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_47.lnote.de.3"/> Pfennige und den dritten Theil<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_47.lnote.de.4"/> eines Pfennigs zur Busse.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone knocks out a person’s eye, let him be given 60 shillings and 6 shillings and 6 pence and a third of a penny as compensation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="87" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone knocks out a man's eye, he shall give him 66 shillings, 6 pence and the third part of a penny as compensation<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_47.attnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="351" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone strikes the eye from a man, he shall be given 60 shillings and 6 shillings and 6 pennies and a third of a penny as compensation.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_19">Leis Wl 19</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>inspired by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_43">Abt 43</ref> <quote>It was Alfred's return to the topic, in making a point that was ... one of Æthelberht's, which argues that the one was inspired by the other (n. 85)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>inspired by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_54">Abt 54–54.5</ref> <quote>It was Alfred's return to the topic, in making a point that was ... one of Æthelberht's, which argues that the one was inspired by the other (n. 85)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>inspired by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_69">Abt 69</ref> <quote>It was Alfred's return to the topic, in making a point that was ... one of Æthelberht's, which argues that the one was inspired by the other (n. 85)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="351"><label>same sum</label> <ref target="clause:Af_71">Af 71</ref> <quote>But the same sum occurs in §75.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="363"><ref target="clause:Af_71">Af 71</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_47.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gesylle <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gesylle Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_47.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">syxtig <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">syxtig Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_47.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ges (<hi rend="italic">Anfang von</hi> geselle) <hi rend="italic">fügt am Zeilenende hier zu, radirt aber aus E</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ges (beginning of geselle) added here at the end of the line, but erased, by E</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_47.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">syx <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">syx Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_47.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">syx pen. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">syx pen. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_47.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">pen. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">pen. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_47.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_47.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_47.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Rasur hinter</hi> i</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">erasure after i</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_47.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">aliquis <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">aliquis Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_47.lnote.oe.4-3" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur Co übergeschr.; fehlt übrigen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above only in Co; lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_47.lnote.oe.5-3" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">81</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">q. est t. <hi rend="italic">fehlt KR;</hi> et trientem I den. <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> et terciam — triens <hi rend="italic">Hn</hi> 93, 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">q. est t. lacking in KR; et trientem I den. instead of et terciam — triens Hn 93, 5</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_47.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">80</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðriddam <hi rend="italic">B</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðriddam B</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_47.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Gliederbussen 5; Auge 2; Hand 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Gliederbussen 5; Auge 2; Hand 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_47.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Aus Abt 43</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">From Abt 43</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_47.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Af meinte jedenfalls ²⁰⁰/₃, wozu ‘6 Pfg.’ in ‘3’ zu korrigieren wäre. Für solche Korrektur spricht erstens, dass statt 66 Schill. 6 Pfg. leichter 67 Schill. 1 Pfg. zu sagen wäre, und dass zweitens ein Schreiberirrtum von II zu U, d. i. 5, oft vorkommt. Allein genau ebenso lautet die Summe doch auch unten 71⁶; möglich also, dass entweder Ælfred beim Diktieren oder bereits vorherige Tradition durch den doppelten Gleichklang 60 + 6 auch zu den 6 Pfg. verführt ward</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Af in any case meant ²⁰⁰/₃, for which ‘6 pence’ would have to be corrected to ‘3’. In favour of such a correction is, first, that instead of 66 shill. 6 pence it would have been easier to say 67 shill. 1 penny, and secondly, that a scribal error turning II into U, i.e. 5, often occurs. But the sum reads exactly the same below in 71⁶; it is possible, therefore, that either Ælfred in dictating or an already existing tradition was led by the double assonance 60 + 6 to the 6 pence as well</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_47.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">61</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">¹/₃ Pfg. (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 7a) kommt ausser bei Af nicht vor</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">¹/₃ penny (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 7a) does not occur except in Af</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_47.attnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">86</biblScope></bibl><label>eage</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">his eage</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_47.attnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">86</biblScope></bibl><label>pæningas</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">peningas</hi>. H. <hi rend="italic">penegas</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Af_47.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Obviously a third of the wergeld (200 shillings) is the amount intended—<hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> 66 shillings, 3 pence and a third part of a penny.</seg></note>
      </div>
